Governments around the globe are working to digitalize their services.
Bolivia is not an exception.
The Bolivian government has been trying to incentivize the use of modern software systems to let users approach bureaucratic processes in a more efficient way.
However, this is not easy to achieve due to the diverse nature of institutions that are part of the government, and the lack of technical knowledge of the people in charge of these institutions.
This project wants to make it easier for the different government institutions to digitalize what we commonly call "Trámites" here in Bolivia.
This work was inspired by prior works on the topic and existing systems used to manage workflows in other contexts, while using Petri Nets as a foundation to model the processes.
